# Design docs: HTML layering + principle diagrams

Applies when the agent writes or substantially revises a technical design (`docs/superpowers/specs/` `§`, or a plan that locks architecture).

## Must deliver (same change)

1. **Core layering** — which process / library owns which lane.
2. **Principle diagram** — data and control flow (stages, thread ownership).
3. **HTML artifact** — self-contained `.html` (inline CSS; optional animation). Prefer Chinese UI labels; keep API names in English.

Markdown may keep a short ASCII sketch. The HTML is the visual. Link it from the spec (`Diagram:` line).

## Placement

`docs/superpowers/diagrams/<topic>.html` — one topic, one file, revise in place.

## Visual style: light technical

| Token | Guidance |
| --- | --- |
| Page bg | `#f4f6f8`–`#fafbfc` |
| Panels | White cards, 1px `#d8dee6` |
| Text | `#1a2330`; muted `#5a6a7e` |
| Accent | `#2563a8` |

No dark-mode default, no CDN, no Mermaid-only substitute.

## Don’t

- Don’t ship an architecture lock with no linked HTML diagram.
- Don’t put diagrams under `ui/` or a second dated design file.
